<title>JAPAN: Japan 1997/98 aluminium product demand seen rising.</title>
<headline>Japan 1997/98 aluminium product demand seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total Japanese demand for aluminium products was forecast to rise a modest 1.0 percent in the fiscal year beginning on April 1, an industry group said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Although demand for mill products was expected to be flat, rising demand from the automobile sector would bring modest growth for aluminium castings and die-cast products, said the group, composed of eight aluminium industry organisations, including the Japan Aluminum Federation and the Japan Aluminium Alloy Refiners' Association.</p>
<p>In a report, it added that low interest rates would fuel continued modest growth in capital expenditures, although this April's increase in the national sales tax was expected to dampen consumer spending and housing construction.</p>
<p>The group's aluminium demand forecasts for 1997/98 and 1996/97 were as follows (in 1,000 tonnes, with percent change from the prior year):</p>
<p>		     1997/98  change  1996/97  change</p>
<p> Mill products   2,311.1   0.0    2,310.7  +5.5</p>
<p> Castings	    407.8  +1.6	401.5  +2.6</p>
<p> Die-cast	    743.4  +2.2	727.3  +5.0</p>
<p> Forgings	     30.3  +2.7	 29.5  +3.1</p>
<p> Cable/wire	   78.0 +48.3	 52.6 -23.8</p>
<p> Steel-related     112.2  -1.0	113.3  -2.7</p>
<p> Powder		 15.5  -1.3	 15.7  -0.6</p>
<p> Imports	     190.5  -0.3	191.0  +4.8</p>
<p> Other		  42.3  +1.9	 41.5   0.0</p>
<p>Domestic total   3,931.1  +1.2    3,883.1  +4.1</p>
<p> Exports	     201.8  -4.0	210.1  -4.1</p>
<p>TOTAL		4,132.9  +1.0    4,093.2  +3.7</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
